WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:02.539
- [Narrator] Located in Romania

00:00:02.539 --> 00:00:05.120
around 400 feet below the town's surface

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.868
is the Salina Turda,

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.221
an underground theme park

00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:11.709
inside one of the oldest
salt mines in the world.

00:00:11.709 --> 00:00:14.292
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:22.028
Salina Turda is believed to
be nearly 2,000 years old.

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:24.400
During its time as a salt mine,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.589
it is estimated that over
three billion tons of salt

00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:29.181
was excavated from the walls

00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:31.681
before mining stopped in 1932.

00:00:34.318 --> 00:00:38.169
This underground hub has
had various uses in the past

00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:39.747
from a cheese storage center

00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:41.940
to a World War II bomb shelter

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.023
but its current usage is
perhaps its most unique.

00:00:48.011 --> 00:00:50.440
In the early 1990s Salina Turda

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.792
was carefully converted

00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:55.292
into a subterranean theme park and museum.

00:00:56.791 --> 00:01:00.269
This active park includes
a 180-seat amphitheater,

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:04.436
an underground lake with
paddle and row boats,

00:01:04.821 --> 00:01:06.238
mini golf course,

00:01:07.111 --> 00:01:11.028
ping pong tables and of
course, a Ferris Wheel.

00:01:13.731 --> 00:01:17.680
Over 2 million people have
visited since its opening.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.150
The dizzying effect of the place

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.590
will leave you feeling
like you've left reality

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.340
in this subterranean wonderland.

